Always reference [implementationTechnical.md](mdc:implementationTechnical.md) for technical specifications. If any technical needs change update this file with the changes.
Always reference [implementationPlan.md](mdc:implementationPlan.md) for functionality requirements. If the user requires any changes to functionality, update this file.
Always update [changelog.md](mdc:changelog.md) with any changes.
Always refer to [database-structure.md](mdc:database-structure.md) for database structure quetions like field names and valid field values. Never assume database structure or field names without refrring to this document.
Never create duplicate functionality
All functions should prioritize logging for debugging and use [class-log-model.php](mdc:models/class-log-model.php). If debugging is on in the main plugin file ('AI_BLOG_GENERATOR_DEBUG' = true) then add extra detailed logs for debugging.
Logs should be written as follows:
    use AI_Blog_Generator\Utilities\Logger;
    Logger::info( 'cron_hooks_registered', 'All cron hooks registered successfully' );
Always use existing methods from other classes
Follow WordPress coding standards strictly
Include proper error handling in every method
Log all important actions and errors
Validate and sanitize all inputs
Escape all outputs
Use dependency injection for class dependencies
Update documentation when making changes.
gpt-image-1 is a valid model from openai. Do not change this at all, and particularly do not replace it with a DALL-E model.
NEVER assume a datatype, functionality or naming convention in a dependency or the database. Always verify the correct functtions, methods, field names when referencing another object.